course: dictionary
lesson: 12815
title: Hard words about care and respect
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are about serious things, and the sentence around them tells you how serious. Embalm means to treat a dead body with special chemicals or salts so it does not rot quickly. «The priests embalmed the king with special salts.» The word salts is a clue: you use salts to keep something from going bad, so embalm must be a careful way of preserving a body.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The family asked the funeral director to embalm their grandmother before the service.» If you put in «to make the body rot faster», the sentence stops making sense, so that meaning is wrong. «To treat the body so it lasts longer» fits, so that is the meaning.
explain: Embalming is a respectful, careful word. You would not use it about cooking or cleaning. It belongs in history lessons about ancient Egypt and in serious talk about funerals, so when you meet it, expect a calm and gentle tone.
fact: Embalm means to treat a dead body so it does not rot quickly.
fact: In ancient Egypt, embalming was part of making a mummy.
fact: Embalmers used special salts, such as natron, to help preserve the body.
fact: Today, a funeral director may embalm a body before a funeral.
fact: The person whose job is embalming is called an embalmer, and the liquid used is called embalming fluid.
exercise: «The funeral director will embalm the body before the service.» What does embalm mean? | To wrap a present in paper | *To treat a dead body so it does not rot quickly | To cook food slowly in an oven | To bury a body deep in the ground
exercise: In ancient Egypt, embalming was part of making a what? | Kite | Pyramid | Boat | *Mummy
exercise: Which word names the person whose job is to embalm bodies? | *Embalmer | Plumber | Glazier | Baker
test: Which sentence uses embalm correctly? | We embalm our sandwiches at lunchtime | The rain will embalm the garden | The cat will embalm the mouse under the table | *The team will embalm the body with special salts
test: In «The priests embalmed the king with special salts», which word is a clue about what was used? | *salts | king | embalmed | priests
exam: Why does a funeral director embalm a body before a funeral? | To hide the body in a jar | *So that it does not rot quickly before the funeral | To make the body wet and heavy | To make the body grow bigger
